====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|hŭn}}, {{IPA|en|/hʌn/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-hon.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌn|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|Hun}}

====Noun====
{{head|en|noun}}

# {{lb|en|used only to address someone}} [[honey|Honey]], [[sweetheart]], {{n-g|a term of endearment}}; {{lb|en|Southern US}}<!--and elsewhere?--> {{n-g|a friendly term of address}}.

===Etymology 2===
{{clipping|en|come on}} with devoicing of /m/. Compare {{m|en|c'mon}}.

====Alternative forms====
* [['hon]], [[h'on]]

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|[m̥ɑn]|/hmɒn/|/hɒn/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒn|s=1}}

====Interjection====
{{en-interj}}

# {{lb|en|Irish|slang}}; {{lb|en|typically}} {{non-gloss definition|cheering a sports team, especially a [[GAA]] team}}; {{non-gloss definition|exhortation or encouragement}} come on; {{non-gloss definition|congratulations}} well done, bravo
#*  '''2013''' September 9, Rosita Boland [https://www.irishtimes.com/sport/gaelic-games/hurling/feelings-of-relief-and-anti-climax-in-ennis-car-park-1.1520448 "Feelings of relief and anti-climax in Ennis car park"] ''The Irish Times''
#*: “'''Hon''' the Banner!” is the single-minded mantra being roared everywhere else.
#*  '''2016''' August 17, Jennifer Dollard [https://www.todayfm.com/AV-Undercover:-Steve-N-Seagulls-cover-Beastie-Boys-Sabotage "Seagulls cover Beastie Boys' 'Sabotage'"] Today FM:
#*: We're not normally impressed by this kind of stuff but '''h'on''' the lads! This is pretty good.
#*  '''2017''' March 16, Amy O'Connor [https://www.dailyedge.ie/gq-dublin-pubs-3290645-Mar2017/ "GQ did a swanky photoshoot in loads of Dublin pubs with the star of Beauty and the Beast"] ''Daily Edge'':
#*: To coincide with the film’s release, GQ recently enlisted the actor to take part in a photoshoot in some of Dublin’s most beloved pubs. ... '''Hon''' Dublin!
#*  '''2017''' April 7, Johnny Watterson, John O'Sullivan, [https://liveblog.irishtimes.com/b276894d85/US-Masters%3A-Day-One/ "Liveblog: US Masters: Day One"] ''The Irish Times'':
#*: 22:23 BIRDIE: Lowry (-2) can't find the bottom of the cup with his eagle putt but taps in for birdie. '''Hon''' the Offalyman. He's one behind the leaders, McGirt and Hoffman

